# WHAT EVERY RANGE'S WIDTH IS MADE OF. One row per narrowing statement anywhere in a filing,
# classified into the thing that would actually reduce it.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THE GRAIN QUESTION, AND IT IS ASKABLE ONLY BECAUSE `narrowsWhen` CARRIES A KIND. How
#    much of the uncertainty in this corpus is IGNORANCE -- a better instrument reveals the
#    number that was always there -- and how much is the world actually MOVING, where no
#    measurement helps and only changing the process does? With no kind to group by, a schema
#    asserts the first reading everywhere, which is the assumption that makes people buy
#    instruments for variation problems.
#
# ⭐⭐ AND `absent/reason = none` IS THE SECOND WAY TO SAY VARIATION. "Somebody looked and
#    nothing would narrow this" is not missing information; it is a finding, and it belongs
#    with `intervention` rather than with the rows nobody has considered.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ AND `absent/reason = derived` IS A THIRD READING THAT IS NEITHER. The width is not in the
#    world at all: it is a function of a SIBLING claim's width, so nothing needs measuring and
#    nothing needs changing, and a receiver holding both already has it. A `booked` share under
#    a clearance is the nameplate less the demand, so it narrows exactly as far as the demand
#    does and never one step further.
#    ⛔ IT WENT UNFILED FOR THE WHOLE OF 0.3.0 AND FIVE CLAIMS SAID IT IN PROSE INSTEAD, typed
#    `instrument` -- a width made of ignorance that a better instrument reveals -- when no
#    instrument is involved and nothing is unmeasured. `tests/state_coverage.rs` had the cell
#    marked incoherent on the ground that there is nothing in a document to derive a narrowing
#    from; there is, whenever a claim is computed from the claims beside it.
#
# ⛔ THE ROWS ARE SCATTERED ACROSS DEMANDS, NAMEPLATES, QUANTA, SLACKS, SHARES, FACTORS AND
#   COUPLING STRENGTHS, because `narrowsWhen` sits on `Claim` and claims are everywhere.
#   Gathering them is what makes the question answerable at the level of a document.
#
# ⭐ AND IT CARRIES THE ELEMENT AND THE MEASURED WIDTH BESIDE THE FILER'S OWN ANSWER,
#   which is what turns a census into something checkable. `no range to narrow` on the last
#   line is the FILER saying so; `is_a_point` is the arithmetic. Two rules compare them.
-- pm:Claim/pm:narrowsWhen, wherever a claim appears.
SELECT n.filing, n.seq, n.owns, n.is_a_point, n.low, n.high, n.unit,
       n.narrows_kind AS kind, n.narrows_absent AS absent, n.narrows_condition AS condition,
       CASE
         WHEN n.narrows_kind = 'instrument'      THEN 'ignorance: measure it better'
         WHEN n.narrows_kind = 'intervention'    THEN 'VARIATION: only changing the process helps'
         WHEN n.narrows_kind = 'experiment'      THEN 'unknown, deliberately: an experiment would say'
         WHEN n.narrows_absent = 'none'          THEN 'VARIATION: somebody looked, nothing would narrow it'
         WHEN n.narrows_absent = 'notApplicable' THEN 'no range to narrow (a point value)'
         ELSE 'nobody has said'
       END AS what_the_width_is_made_of
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/claims.sqlc)
) n
